---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/config/site';
import { getProducts } from '@/lib/products';
import { breadcrumbSchema, organizationSchema, jsonLdGraph } from '@/lib/seo';

const all = await getProducts();
const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'How We Rank', url: '/how-we-rank' },
];
const jsonLd = jsonLdGraph(organizationSchema(), breadcrumbSchema(crumbs));
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How We Rank Soldering Kits and Tools"
  description="Our editorial process: what we weigh when ranking soldering kits, irons and accessories, how our scores are built, what our reviews are not, and how affiliate links are handled."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <div class="container-px py-8 lg:py-12">
    <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
    <div class="prose prose-lg mx-auto mt-8 max-w-3xl">
      <h1>How we rank soldering kits and tools</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        {SITE.name} currently covers {all.length} products. This page explains exactly how those
        rankings are made, what our scores mean, and — just as importantly — what our reviews are
        not.
      </p>

      <h2>What our reviews are, and what they are not</h2>
      <p>
        Our reviews are <strong>research-based editorial assessments</strong>. We do not run a
        laboratory, and we do not claim to have bench-tested every product on this site. Saying
        otherwise would be easy and dishonest, and it is exactly the kind of claim that makes
        affiliate sites untrustworthy.
      </p>
      <p>What we do instead:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Read the full specification and what is actually in the box, from the live listing.</li>
        <li>Compare each product against every direct alternative we cover, not against a vacuum.</li>
        <li>Weigh the pattern of owner feedback — recurring complaints matter more than single reviews.</li>
        <li>Apply hands-on soldering knowledge: which tip shapes, wattages and features matter in practice, and which are marketing.</li>
        <li>Name the weaknesses. Every review lists cons, and every roundup entry carries a "watch out for" line.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we weigh</h2>
      <h3>For kits</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Instructions</strong> — the single biggest predictor of whether someone finishes a kit.</li>
        <li><strong>The finished result</strong> — a gadget worth keeping beats a board you throw away.</li>
        <li><strong>Technique taught</strong> — through-hole fundamentals, surface-mount practice, or both.</li>
        <li><strong>Joint count and difficulty</strong> — matched to who the kit is for.</li>
        <li><strong>What you still have to buy</strong> — most kits do not include an iron or solder.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>For irons, stations and accessories</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Temperature control</strong> — regulated heat is the difference between consistent joints and guesswork.</li>
        <li><strong>Heat recovery</strong> — wattage matters on big joints; peak temperature rarely does.</li>
        <li><strong>Tips</strong> — availability, shapes and cost over the life of the tool.</li>
        <li><strong>What is included</strong> — a cheap station with helping hands and consumables can beat a pricier bare one.</li>
        <li><strong>Safety</strong> — ESD-safe designs, stands, and fume handling.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How the score works</h2>
      <p>
        Every product carries a score out of 10. It is an editorial judgement of how well that
        product serves <em>the person it is for</em>, not an absolute measure of quality — a budget
        kit aimed at a first-timer and a professional station are scored against different
        expectations. Ranked lists are ordered by that score, with our stated award (Best Overall,
        Best Budget, and so on) explaining the role each product plays.
      </p>
      <p>
        Scores change when the facts change: if a listing drops accessories, a model is revised, or
        a better alternative arrives, the ranking is updated and the date on the page changes with it.
      </p>

      <h2>Why there are no prices on the site</h2>
      <p>
        Amazon prices move constantly, and a price printed on a review page is wrong almost
        immediately. Rather than show a stale number, every product links to its current listing.
        Our price tiers ($, $$, $$$) give you the rough bracket so you can plan a budget.
      </p>

      <h2>How affiliate links work here</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.name} is funded by affiliate commissions. As an Amazon Associate we earn from
        qualifying purchases, at no extra cost to you. Commission rates do not vary enough between
        these products to make any of them worth promoting over another, and rankings are set before
        links are added. Our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure">affiliate disclosure</a> has the full
        detail.
      </p>

      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        If something here is wrong — a specification, a claim about what is in the box, or a product
        that has changed since we wrote about it — tell us and we will fix it. Accuracy matters more
        to us than any single recommendation. Use the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
